// Test: bugfixes/ssr_concat_conditional_helper_no_oom
// Grammar: while_statement, if_statement, variable_declaration, assignment, binary_expression
// Semantic: COM001 (tracking: CMP-SSR-MALLOC-OOM-PAGE-RENDER-CACHE-INEFFECTIVE,
//                  CMP-SSR-MALLOC-OOM-CONDITIONAL-HELPER)
//
// Guards a per-iteration HTML-section build pattern in which the outer
// accumulator (`acc = acc + ...`) is interleaved with three conditional
// helper locals declared inside the loop body (`string headHtml = ""`,
// then `if head != "" headHtml = "<h2>" + head + "</h2>"`).
//
// The combined shape OOM'd the bump allocator on real SSR pages
// (Web Site Clean /syntax, /tutorials). The 0.30.368 chained-RHS
// matcher rewrites the outer `acc = acc + e1 + e2 + ... + eN` into a
// doubling-capacity StringBuilder, but the surrounding conditional
// helpers (`headHtml = "<h2>" + head + "</h2>"` etc.) continued to
// allocate via plain `string.concat` and stranded in the bump heap.
// Across N iterations the leak grows as ~ 50 bytes × N and trips the
// 128 MB bump cap on /tutorials at ~30 iterations.
//
// 0.30.373/0.30.374 tried to fix the helper leak by emitting a
// `string_builder_reclaim` call at the end of the body. That regressed
// to CMP-SSR-RECLAIM-FREES-LIVE-POINTER because the end-of-body
// placement corrupts cross-iter live pointers (e.g. `head = json.get(...)`
// at the bottom of a `while head != ""` loop). The reclaim emission
// was reverted; the chained-RHS rewrite remains and still resolves the
// dominant CMP-SSR-MALLOC-OOM-PAGE-RENDER case (turning the
// accumulator from O(n²) into O(n) heap). The conditional-helper leak
// is bounded per render (a few KB on /tutorials) and the json.get
// parse-tree cache from 0.30.369 keeps it from dominating heap
// pressure.
//
// This test just guards correctness: 5000 iters of the conditional-helper
// shape compile and run to completion with the expected length.
//
// Expected output:
//   265000

start:
	string acc = ""
	integer i = 0
	while i < 5000
		string head = "H"
		string body = "B"
		string foot = "F"
		string headHtml = ""
		if head != ""
			headHtml = "<h2>" + head + "</h2>"
		string bodyHtml = ""
		if body != ""
			bodyHtml = "<p>" + body + "</p>"
		string footHtml = ""
		if foot != ""
			footHtml = "<small>" + foot + "</small>"
		acc = acc + "<section>" + headHtml + bodyHtml + footHtml + "</section>"
		i = i + 1
	printl(acc.length().toString())
